   'Body mass index is a quick screening number used worldwide by doctors and public health agencies. It is calculated by dividing weight in kilograms by height in metres squared. It is useful for spotting general trends, but it is only one piece of information, so treat the result as a starting point for a conversation with a health professional rather than a verdict.'
