 art:{
  intro:[
   'The Unit Converter changes a measurement from one unit to another as you type. It covers seven everyday categories: length, weight, temperature, area, volume, speed and data storage, with metric, imperial and binary units. Choose a category, enter a value, pick the units and the answer appears immediately, together with a table showing the same value in every other unit of that category.',
   'Recipes, travel plans, school homework, shipping forms and engineering drawings all mix measuring systems, and file sizes bring their own confusion between decimal units like megabytes and binary units like mebibytes. Converting by memory leads to mistakes, especially with temperature, area and data storage, where the numbers are not always a simple round factor. This converter uses standard international conversion factors and performs the arithmetic in your browser, so it is fast, works offline once loaded and never sends your numbers anywhere.'
  ],
  steps:[
   'Pick a category from the tabs: Length, Weight, Temperature, Area, Volume, Speed or Data Storage.',
   'Type the number you want to convert into the <strong>Value</strong> box.',
   'Choose the starting unit in <strong>From</strong> and the target unit in <strong>To</strong>. Use the swap button to reverse them.',
