   'Compressing JSON to reduce size before storing or sending it.',
   'Finding the exact position of a stray comma, quote or bracket.',
   'Sorting keys to compare two JSON documents more easily.'
  ],
  faqs:[
   ['What are the most common JSON mistakes?','Trailing commas after the last item, single quotes instead of double quotes, unquoted property names, comments and missing brackets are the usual causes. JSON is stricter than JavaScript object syntax.'],
   ['Why does the error position sometimes point a little after the real mistake?','Parsers report where they realized something was wrong, which can be just after the actual mistake. Check the reported spot and the characters immediately before it.'],
   ['Does formatting change my data?','No. Beautifying and minifying change only whitespace. Sorting keys changes the order of properties in objects, but not their values. Arrays keep their original order.'],
   ['Is there a size limit?','There is no fixed limit, but very large files depend on your device memory. Documents of several megabytes usually format in a moment on a modern computer.'],
   ['Is my JSON uploaded anywhere?','No. Parsing and formatting happen entirely in your browser, so sensitive tokens, personal data and internal configuration never leave your device.']
  ]
 }
